# E §4.2 step 5: in step 3, "each reading that follows one, as they are booked" is tested, and "that reading's pad" is
# refused (RUN-PLACE); "A refused leg isn't booked". The decision p puts 10.00 PLN into a (110.00 PLN); a reading after
# it states 140.00 PLN, a pad of 30.00 PLN out of the claim y (at 0): refused. snap11 refused the pad and still counted
# the reading's end in the conservation check, ENGINE-INVARIANT (writer 8, sixth pass, found beside C2-1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
source bk "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place a: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place y: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input day: date

move p: transfers
  on day
  reads a
  leg cash from world to a amount amt + 0 * bal(a)

ask q: bal(y, 2026-03-31), bal(a, 2026-03-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  day = 2026-03-10
  opening[a] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[y] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version st
  cite bk
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  pad a from y
  stated[a] = 140.00 PLN after p
=== expect
q: (refused: RUN-PLACE pads:st:a@after p takes y below 0, refused: RUN-PLACE pads:st:a@after p takes y below 0)
  pad: a after p, pads:st:a@after p of 30.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
